.TH MOUNT_CDFS 1M "3 November 2026" "cdfs"
.SH NAME
mount_cdfs \- mount a CD with the cdfs filesystem
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mount \-F cdfs
[
.B \-o
.I options
]
.IB card , unit
.I directory
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cdfs
is a read-only filesystem for CD and DVD media: ISO 9660 (with Rock Ridge
and Joliet), UDF and HFS.
The filesystem is a kernel module, from the package
.B cdfs-k30
or
.BR cdfs-k46 ,
whichever matches the running kernel; it loads at the first cdfs mount.
This package installs the mount helper,
.BR /usr/lib/fs/cdfs/mount ,
which
.BR mount (1M)
runs for
.BR "\-F cdfs" ,
and the mount point
.BR /cdrom .
.PP
The drive is named by its SCSI controller and target, not by a
.B /dev
path:
.I card
is the controller's index and
.I unit
the drive's target id, joined by any character that is not a digit
.RB ( 0,2 ,
.B 0.2
and
.B 0:2
are the same drive).
Give
.I directory
as an absolute path.
.PP
The helper always mounts read-only and ignores any
.B \-o
options.
It then adds the mount to
.BR /etc/mnttab ,
with the mount point in the special field as well as in the mount point
field, as for
.B /proc
and
.BR /dev/fd .
So
.B mount
and
.B df
show the CD as
.IR "directory " on " directory" ,
not by its drive, and
.BI "umount " directory
unmounts it and removes the entry.
.SH EXAMPLES
Mount the CD in the drive at target 2 of the first controller, list it and
unmount it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mount \-F cdfs 0,2 /cdrom
ls /cdrom
umount /cdrom
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP 24
.B /usr/lib/fs/cdfs/mount
the helper; this directory must hold no other file
.TP
.B /etc/mnttab
the table of mounted filesystems
.TP
.B /cdrom
the usual mount point
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status 0: mounted.
If the mount worked but
.B /etc/mnttab
could not be written, the helper prints a warning and still exits 0;
the CD stays mounted.
Exit status 1: the mount failed, with the errno printed:
.TP 10
.B ENXIO
no controller at that
.IR card .
.TP
.B ENOTTY
the target answers but is not a CD drive; check
.IR unit .
.TP
.B EINVAL
no filesystem cdfs reads on the disc, a disc of a shape it does not
serve, or a spec that is not
.IR card , unit .
.TP
.B EIO
the drive delivered no readable data: cable, termination or media.
.TP
.B EBUSY
that drive or that directory is already mounted.
.TP
.B ENOMEM
a kernel allocation failed.
.TP
.B EPERM
not the superuser.
.TP
.B ENOTDIR
.I directory
is not a directory.
.PP
Exit status 2: fewer than two operands.
.PP
.B mount
reports
.B "unknown fstype"
or fails at once when the cdfs module is not installed or the kernel
cannot load it.
.SH NOTES
A file named
.B umount
in
.B /usr/lib/fs/cdfs
breaks
.BR umount (1M)
for cdfs mounts
.RB ( "cannot execute" ,
the CD stays mounted): remove it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mount (1M),
.BR umount (1M),
.BR mnttab (4)
